      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SOUTH AUSSIE STAR (2) made a nice return at her latest appearance two weeks ago, finishing a neck away in second over 1800m at this track. A nice draw on the front line should ensure a cosy run. Steps up a level but she is fitter and up to the task. LEVIOSA (3) is a three-year-old filly by Stay Hungry from Delacour on debut. Will enjoy a nice run from this favourable starting position. Placed in a recent trial and makes plenty of appeal. JADES REASON (5) was responsible for a better effort last time out when third over 1800m at this venue. Should run a big race. SAL WESTER (9) is in the mix following a respectable second at her most recent appearance over 1609m at Port Pirie. May earn some minor money.",
